       All routines return the integer EERRRR upon failure and an  integer  value
       other  than  EERRRR  upon successful completion, unless otherwise noted in
       the preceding routine descriptions.

       X/Open Curses does not specify any error conditions.  In this implemen‐
       tation

          iiss__lliinneettoouucchheedd
               returns  an error if the window pointer is null, or if the line
               number is outside the window boundaries.

               The constant EERRRR is distinct from TTRRUUEE and FFAALLSSEE, which are the
               normal  return  values  of this function.  Because the function
               returns a bbooooll, returning EERRRR (which is neither TTRRUUEE nor FFAALLSSEE)
               may not be supported by the compiler.

               To  provide  error-checking  and also match the X/Open function
               prototype, the EERRRR is provided by a macro named iiss__lliinneettoouucchheedd.
               The actual function returns FFAALLSSEE when it detects an error.

          wwttoouucchhllnn
               returns  an error if the window pointer is null, or if the line
               number is outside the window boundaries.

